<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marienkirche, Reutlingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1247–<a href="/years/1343">1343</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marienkirche in Reutlingen is a Gothic church built between about 1247 and 1343, the city's main church and a symbol of its time as a free imperial city. It was badly damaged in the great town fire of 1726 and restored in the 19th century.</p></div>
